{"type": "message", "id": "ba96e4fd", "parentId": "7234ad55", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:14.343Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:0", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"most deadly cancers 5 year survival rates 2024\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 995,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2dac914cdd25d27\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer survival rates | Nuffield Trust\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2dac914cdd25d27\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nuffieldtrust.org.uk/resource/cancer-survival-rates\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dac2162879215a71\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe cancers with the lowest five-year ... survival estimates were seen in patients with <strong>testicular cancer (93.5%), melanoma of skin (92.6%) and prostate cancer (88.5%).</strong>...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dac2162879215a71\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nuffieldtrust.org.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0159e5885d8dfe3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0159e5885d8dfe3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/common.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c5a0b3e053dd5f41\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Lung and bronchus cancer</strong> is responsible for the most deaths with 124,730 people expected to die from this disease. That is nearly three times the 52,900 deaths due to colorectal cancer, which is the second most common cause of cancer death.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c5a0b3e053dd5f41\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9945a9daf290b3f5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer survival rates - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9945a9daf290b3f5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cancer_survival_rates\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"99c3625df28f2592\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Small cell lung cancer</strong> has a five-year survival rate of 4% according to Cancer Centers of America&#x27;s Website. The American Cancer Society reports 5-year relative survival rates of over 70% for women with stage 0-III breast cancer with a 5-year relative survival rate close to 100% for women with ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"99c3625df28f2592\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 31, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b1a2d4d758c1ad50\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhat Are the Deadliest Cancers?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b1a2d4d758c1ad50\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.verywellhealth.com/top-deadliest-cancers-1123927\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6dd9c3a18c0115e8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most deadly types of cancers include <strong>lung, colon, pancreatic cancer, breast, and prostate cancers</strong>. Keep in mind that estimated deaths can vary between males and females and may be affected by age and family history.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6dd9c3a18c0115e8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 14, 2015\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.verywellhealth.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3182e0b2635398e8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Survival Rate: Understanding Your Prognosis\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3182e0b2635398e8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/cancer-survival-rate\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a7244fafdd47c14\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA cancer survival rate is an estimate of the chance that you’ll be alive five years after receiving a cancer diagnosis, but not how long you’ll live. Read on to learn more.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a7244fafdd47c14\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 29, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"my.clevelandclinic.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"396dda8b04a711c9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMost Dangerous Cancers in Men and Women\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"396dda8b04a711c9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.unitypoint.org/news-and-articles/most-dangerous-cancers-in-men-and-women\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4cb817694b4dffc9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPancreas Because <strong>pancreatic cancer</strong> progresses rapidly, and no method of early detection is currently available, it’s one of the most dangerous types of cancer. The incidence rate has increased by about 1% per year since 2000.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4cb817694b4dffc9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.unitypoint.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87e6fe3bda1d2b5a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87e6fe3bda1d2b5a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5d30520228020d7e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable 8.