{"type": "message", "id": "1489ebe5", "parentId": "43c52473", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:14.374Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:2", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"cancer survival rates United States overview statistics\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 981,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"855a353a79b32468\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Statistics - NCI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"855a353a79b32468\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/understanding/statistics\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"085c64cb6296afb3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhen comparing groups based on ... Asian/Pacific Islander women (83.1 per 100,000). <strong>As of January 2022, there were an estimated 18.1 million cancer survivors in the United States</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"085c64cb6296afb3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df114d82c0fa09fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nACS Annual Statistics Report: Milestone 70 Percent 5-Year Survival Rate for all Cancers Combined; Largest Gains for Advanced and Fatal Cancers\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df114d82c0fa09fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pressroom.cancer.org/cancer-statistics-report-2026\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5925ea50c72251dd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>In 2026 in the U.S., approximately 2,114,850 new cancer diagnoses (5,800 each day) are projected to occur, and 626,140 people will die from the disease</strong>. Although the cancer mortality rate has continued to decline through 2023, dropping by a ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5925ea50c72251dd\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pressroom.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7d77a9af7887a55\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStatistics and Graphs | Division of Cancer Control and Population Sciences (DCCPS)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a7d77a9af7887a55\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://cancercontrol.cancer.gov/ocs/statistics\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f238e8607c34ad8b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>In 2018, there were 623,405 people living with metastatic breast, prostate, lung, colorectal, or bladder cancer or metastatic melanoma in the United States</strong>. That number has been estimated to increase to over 693,400 by 2025.3 ... Female breast cancer survivors represent 23% of cancer survivors ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f238e8607c34ad8b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"cancercontrol.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c72b6b84fdad8365\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer survival in the United States 2007–2016: Results from the National Program of Cancer Registries - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c72b6b84fdad8365\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10174513/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"64cd5183bd12b4f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis analysis provided a high-level overview of contemporary cancer survival in the United States. Even though cancer incidence rates stabilized during 2013 to 2016 among males and increased slightly among females, cancer death rates continued to decline steadily among both males and females [1]. Changes in incidence and mortality reflect, in part, changes in cancer risk factors and screening and imaging 