al rate for mesothelioma is about <strong>10%</strong> – meaning about <strong>10%</strong> of patients survive beyond 5 years after a mesothelioma diagnosis.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"abe2c988e8378633\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 24, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"mesotheliomahub.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a271b462902dc1c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancers with Low Survival Rates: Which Ones Have Poor Prognosis?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5a271b462902dc1c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://eucee.in/cancers-with-low-survival-rates-which-ones-have-poor-prognosis\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e346c33be5aed45\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe five‑year survival for pancreatic, lung (small cell), mesothelioma, glioblastoma, liver, esophageal and certain ovarian cancers is <strong>under 20%</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e346c33be5aed45\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 9, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"eucee.in\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "mesothelioma glioblastoma esophageal cancer liver cancer stomach cancer 5 year survival rates", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1143, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c1b44d57e3ebea12\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Survival Rates by Type and Stage | American Cancer Fund\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c1b44d57e3ebea12\">>>", "url": "https://americancancerfund.org/cancer-survival-rates/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e553b2fcc88b482c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>Liver cancer: approximately 22% overall 5-year survival rate</strong>. Esophageal cancer: approximately 22% overall 5-year survival rate. Pancreatic cancer: approximately 13% overall 5-year survi