{"type": "message", "id": "1455aafa", "parentId": "19dfbd43", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:22.424Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:5", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"chordoma retinoblastoma Merkel cell carcinoma neuroendocrine tumor annual cases US\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 978,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e89da8f2d85cf7fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMerkel Cell Carcinoma - PMC - NIH\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e89da8f2d85cf7fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5443625/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"735c56ebd797359b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOverall, the 5-year disease-specific survival (DSS) rate for MCC is estimated to be <strong>between 30% and 64%</strong>,1 with a DSS rate greater than 90% for those with local disease.2 It is thus clear that the timely and accurate diagnosis of this aggressive primary cutaneous neuroendocrine carcinoma (NEC) ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"735c56ebd797359b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db0dcf7f747d50fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMerkel Cell Carcinoma of the Skin - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db0dcf7f747d50fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482329/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d23d114e1149004a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMCC is a rare but highly aggressive ... stage at presentation. Reported <strong>5-year overall survival rates are approximately 55% to 60% for localized disease, 35% to 40% for regional nodal involvement, and 15% or lower for distant metastatic disease</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d23d114e1149004a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 6, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"819c6b0c54eddb73\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCutaneous neuroendocrine (Merkel cell) carcinoma. A report of 35 cases - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"819c6b0c54eddb73\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7747706/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f2252a42756014e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe medical records of <strong>35 patients</strong> diagnosed with CNEC and treated at Southern California Kaiser Permanente Medical Group or UCLA Medical Center between 1980 and 1991 were reviewed.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f2252a42756014e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a098b810406063eb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMetastatic Neuroendocrine Neoplasms of Unknown Primary: Clues from Pathology Workup\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a098b810406063eb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2072-6694/14/9/2210\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"21968557c3eaa21a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNeuroendocrine neoplasms (NENs) are diverse tumors arising in various anatomical locations and may therefore cause a variety of symptoms leading to their discovery. However, there are instances in which a NEN first presents clinically as a metastatic deposit, while the associated primary tumor ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"21968557c3eaa21a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 28, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdpi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n     