{"type": "message", "id": "9f87a48e", "parentId": "a4e7d98e", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:32.018Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:6", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"glioblastoma 5 year survival rate statistics\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1125,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e71a740e8cd1ea9a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhat is the average glioblastoma survival rate? — Glioblastoma Research Organization\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e71a740e8cd1ea9a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gbmresearch.org/blog/glioblastoma-survival-rate\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f937002491b6cfbb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA five-year relative glioblastoma survival rate means that people who have that tumor are, on average, about <strong>6.8%</strong> as likely as people who don&#x27;t have that tumor to live for at least five years after being diagnosed.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f937002491b6cfbb\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 1, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gbmresearch.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88298c894ffed48d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEpidemiology and Outcome of Glioblastoma - Glioblastoma - NCBI Bookshelf\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"88298c894ffed48d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470003/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05a625d09e561d58\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUse of anti-inflammatory medication has been found to be protective against GBM. Survival from GBM is poor; only few patients survive 2.5 years and <strong>less than 5%</strong> of patients survive 5 years following diagnosis. Survival rates for patients with GBM have shown no notable improvement in population ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05a625d09e561d58\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 27, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32658d70288cdbd9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma: Clinical Presentation, Multidisciplinary Management, and Long-Term Outcomes - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32658d70288cdbd9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11719842/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a14aeec458f43e63\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDespite these interventions, median survival remains approximately 12–15 months, with a five-year survival rate <strong>below 10%</strong>. Prognosis is influenced by factors such as patient age, molecular characteristics, and the extent of resection. Patients with IDH-mutant tumors or methylated MGMT promoters ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a14aeec458f43e63\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95c65869423cddad\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma and Increased Survival with Longer Chemotherapy Duration - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"95c65869423cddad\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6710024/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4320dce7bd74524\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n(CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/) ... The five-year survival rate for patients with glioblastoma (GBM) is low at <strong>approximately 4.7%</strong>. Radiotherapy plus concomitant and adjuvant temozolomide (TMZ) remains the standard of care