rm-survivors\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e07cbfb3366e90c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAs mentioned earlier, the median ... that these are medians, and individual experiences can differ significantly. In fact, <strong>around 6.9%</strong> of patients reach the five-year survival mark....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e07cbfb3366e90c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 27, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aaroncohen-gadol.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f3a11e8d9f1dafb4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLonger-term (≥ 2 years) survival in patients with glioblastoma in population-based studies pre- and post-2005: a systematic review and meta-analysis | Scientific Reports\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f3a11e8d9f1dafb4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-68011-4\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ceeb8cea16f73e2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n... Glioblastoma multiforme is the most common primary malignant brain tumour in adults with an incidence rate of <strong>3.7 per 100,000 person-years</strong>, though geographical variation exists1.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ceeb8cea16f73e2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 15, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nature.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "glioblastoma 5 year survival rate statistics", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1125, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e71a740e8cd1ea9a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhat is the average glioblastoma survival rate? — Glioblastoma Research Organization\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e71a740e8cd1ea9a\">>>", "url": "https://www.gbmresearch.org/blog/glioblastoma-survival-rate", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f937002491b6cfbb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA five-year relative glioblastoma survival rate means that people who have that tumor are, on average, about <strong>6.8%</strong> as likely as people who don&#x27;t have that tumor to live for at least five years after being diagnosed.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f937002491b6cfbb\">>>", "published": "December 1, 2022", "siteName": "www.gbmresearch.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"88298c894ffed48d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEpidemiology and Outcome of Glioblastoma - Glioblastoma - NCBI Bookshelf\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"88298c894ffed48d\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470003/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05a625d09e561d58\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nUse of anti-inflammatory medication has been found to be protective against GBM. Survival from GBM is poor; only few patients survive 2.5 years and <strong>less than 5%</strong> of patients survive 5 years following diagnosis. Survival rates for patients with GBM have shown no notable improvement in population ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05a625d09e561d58\">>>", "published": "September 27, 2017", "siteName": "www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"32658d70288cdbd9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma: Clinical Presentation, Multidisciplinary Management, and Long-Term Outcomes - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"32658d70288cdbd9\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11719842/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a14aeec458f43e63\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDespite these interventions, median survival remains approximately 12–15 months, with a five-year survival rate <strong>below 10%</strong>. Prognosis is influenced by factors such as patient age, molecular characteristics, and the extent of resection. Patients with IDH-mutant tumors or methylated MGMT promoters ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a14aeec458f43e63\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"95c65869423cddad\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma and Increased Survival with Longer Chemotherapy Duration - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"95c65869423cddad\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6710024/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e4320dce7bd74524\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n(CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/) ... The five-year survival rate for patients with glioblastoma (GBM) is low at <strong>approximately 4.7%</strong>. Radiotherapy plus concomitant and adjuvant temozolomide (TMZ) remains the standard of care.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e4320dce7bd74524\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3700b6959d144f4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma Survival Rate | Glioblastoma Foundation News\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3700b6959d144f4\">>>", "url": "https://glioblastomafoundation.org/news/glioblastoma-multiforme/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"657ade02c2829704\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt is estimated that more than 10,000 individuals in the United States will succumb to glioblastoma every year. The five-year survival rate for glioblastoma patients is only <strong>6.9 percent</strong>, and the average length of survival for glioblastoma patients ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"657ade02c2829704\">>>", "published": "August 30, 2021", "siteName": "glioblastomafoundation.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"204bef15783485c3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma Prognosis | Survival Rates\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"204bef15783485c3\">>>", "url": "https://www.thebraintumourcharity.org/brain-tumour-diagnosis-treatment/types-of-brain-tum