, 2024", "siteName": "link.springer.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2319e5240be2c8e4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma Survival: Expert Advice, Aaron Cohen-Gadol, MD | Aaron Cohen-Gadol, MD\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2319e5240be2c8e4\">>>", "url": "https://www.aaroncohen-gadol.com/en/patients/glioma/survival/long-term-survivors", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e07cbfb3366e90c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAs mentioned earlier, the median ... that these are medians, and individual experiences can differ significantly. In fact, <strong>around 6.9%</strong> of patients reach the five-year survival mark....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e07cbfb3366e90c\">>>", "published": "April 27, 2022", "siteName": "www.aaroncohen-gadol.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f3a11e8d9f1dafb4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLonger-term (≥ 2 years) survival in patients with glioblastoma in population-based studies pre- and post-2005: a systematic review and meta-analysis | Scientific Reports\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f3a11e8d9f1dafb4\">>>", "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-68011-4", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ceeb8cea16f73e2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n... Glioblastoma multiforme is the most common primary malignant brain tumour in adults with an incidence rate of <strong>3.7 per 100,000 person-years</strong>, though geographical variation exists1.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9ceeb8cea16f73e2\">>>", "published": "July 15, 2020", "siteName": "www.nature.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349052017}}
{"type": "message", "id": "19a79c82", "parentId": "9f87a48e", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:32.019Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:7", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"chordoma annual cases United States incidence\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1010,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"abed297865234d8f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDescriptive epidemiology of chordomas in the United States - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"abed297865234d8f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32342333/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bcf448df210c6ffe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most common location was cranial (38.7%), followed by sacral (34.3%) and spinal (27.0%). The average age-adjusted incidence rate was <strong>0.088 per 100,000 persons per year</strong> (95% CI 0.086-0.091), with an annual percentage change of 1.29% (95% ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bcf448df210c6ffe\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef463f83758d6c5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: Practice Essentials, History of the Disease, Epidemiology\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef463f83758d6c5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/250902-overview\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be7c91c5d21fea93\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in children and in adults, with an incidence of approximately <strong>350 cases per year</strong> in the United States [6] and a reported annual worldwide incidence of 0.08 per 100,000 cases.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"be7c91c5d21fea93\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"emedicine.medscape.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74086832af5bdb0f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: incidence and survival patterns in the United States, 1973-1995 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74086832af5bdb0f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11227920/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2344ff51643974a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults: The age-adjusted chordoma incidence rate (IR) of <strong>0.08 per 100,000</strong> was age-dependent, more common in males (IR 0.10) than females (IR 0.06) and rare among patients aged &lt;40 years and blacks.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a2344ff51643974a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"989d4b2c45febe21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: New Updates and Breakthroughs 2024\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"989d4b2c45febe21\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://oncodaily.com/oncolibrary/cancer-types/chordoma-in-adults-76224\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7701452e51765fb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the United States, the annual incidence is <strong>about 350 cases</strong>, translating to roughly 1 per million people. These tumors account for 1% to 4% of all primary bone malignancies and about 20% of primary spinal tumors.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c7701452e51765fb\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 31, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"oncodaily.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3db6d5266b16772\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: Current status, problems, and future directions - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3db6d5266b16772\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S014702722100088X\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba1760771a94b4a3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in pediatrics and adults, with an incidence of <strong>approximately 350 cases per year</strong> in the United States. While typically described as slow-growing, many patients will eventually develop ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba1760771a94b4a3\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 1, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"01ff4eb546734534\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: The Quest for Better Treatment Options - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"01ff4eb546734534\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5315072/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b0d8a7de8a5ef8bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is an extremely rare cancer, with an incidence of about <strong>one case per million persons per year</strong> in the USA and Europe (about 300 and 450 cases per year, respectively). The estimated median overall survival of patients with chordoma is approximately 6–7 years, yielding a rough estimate ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b0d8a7de8a5ef8bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbbaf5378c63191b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPopulation-based survival analysis of primary spinal chordoma in the US from 2000 to 2020 - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbbaf5378c63191b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11538232/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ed0b2dba8205feb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordomas are rare, slow-growing, ... and vascular structures. The annual incidence rate of new chordoma diagnoses is approximately <strong>one to two cases per million each year</strong>, with a slightly higher frequency in males than females [2]....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4ed0b2dba8205feb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c42916631fb5ced\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncidence, Management, and Outcomes of Adult Spinal Chordoma Patients in the United States - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6c42916631fb5ced\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9972264/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78a411bab1fe64f2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSpinal chordomas are malignant neoplasms of the primitive notochord that have an incidence of approximately <strong>five out of one million cases per year</strong>.1-5 Chordomas are located on the axial skeleton, specifically in the sacrum (50-60%), skull base (25-35%), cervical region (10%), and thoracolumbar ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78a411bab1fe64f2\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87205033eb29e0a0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma | Diagnosis & Disease Information - Cancer Therapy Advisor\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87205033eb29e0a0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancertherapyadvisor.com/ddi/chordoma/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bbaf5f6009e915b5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma accounts for approximately 1% to 4% of all primary bone tumors.3 In the United States (US), the estimated annual incidence of chordoma is roughly <strong>1 case per 1 million people</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bbaf5f6009e915b5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 16, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancertherapyadvisor.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"126749b77ad23fc5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"126749b77ad23fc5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chordoma\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c24813eb3b1cea1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWith appropriate treatment, many chordoma patients will live for a decade or more, and some can be cured. In the United States, the annual incidence of chordoma is approximately <strong>1 in one million</strong> (300 new patients each year).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7c24813eb3b1cea1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 22, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "chordoma annual cases United States incidence", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1010, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"abed297865234d8f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDescriptive epidemiology of chordomas in the United States - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"abed297865234d8f\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32342333/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bcf448df210c6ffe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe most common location was cranial (38.7%), followed by sacral (34.3%) and spinal (27.0%). The average age-adjusted incidence rate was <strong>0.088 per 100,000 persons per year</strong> (95% CI 0.086-0.091), with an annual percentage change of 1.29% (95% ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bcf448df210c6ffe\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ef463f83758d6c5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: Practice Essentials, History of the Disease, Epidemiology\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ef463f83758d6c5\">>>", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/250902-overview", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be7c91c5d21fea93\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in children and in adults, with an incidence of approximately <strong>350 cases per year</strong> in the United States [6] and a reported annual worldwide incidence of 0.08 per 100,000 cases.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"be7c91c5d21fea93\">>>", "siteName": "emedicine.medscape.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"74086832af5bdb0f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: incidence and survival patterns in the United States, 1973-1995 - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"74086832af5bdb0f\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11227920/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a2344ff51643974a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nResults: The age-adjusted chordoma incidence rate (IR) of <strong>0.08 per 100,000</strong> was age-dependent, more common in males (IR 0.10) than females (IR 0.06) and rare among patients aged &lt;40 years and blacks.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a2344ff51643974a\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"989d4b2c45febe21\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: New Updates and Breakthroughs 2024\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"989d4b2c45febe21\">>>", "url": "https://oncodaily.com/oncolibrary/cancer-types/chordoma-in-adults-76224", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7701452e51765fb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn the United States, the annual incidence is <strong>about 350 cases</strong>, translating to roughly 1 per million people. These tumors account for 1% to 4% of all primary bone malignancies and about 20% of primary spinal tumors.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7701452e51765fb\">>>", "published": "October 31, 2025", "siteName": "oncodaily.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3db6d5266b16772\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: Current status, problems, and future directions - ScienceDirect\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3db6d5266b16772\">>>", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S014702722100088X", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba1760771a94b4a3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in pediatrics and adults, with an incidence of <strong>approximately 350 cases per year</strong> in the United States. While typically described as slow-growing, many patients will eventually develop ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba1760771a94b4a3\">>>", "published": "July 1, 2021", "siteName": "www.sciencedirect.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"01ff4eb546734534\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma: The Quest for Better Treatment Options - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"01ff4eb546734534\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5315072/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b0d8a7de8a5ef8bb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma is an extremely rare cancer, with an incidence of about <strong>one case per million persons per year</strong> in the USA and Europe (about 300 and 450 cases per year, respectively). The estimated median overall survival of patients with chordoma is approximately 6–7 years, yielding a rough estimate ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b0d8a7de8a5ef8bb\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fbbaf5378c63191b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPopulation-based survival analysis of primary spinal chordoma in the US from 2000 to 2020 - 