strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bbaf5f6009e915b5\">>>", "published": "July 16, 2025", "siteName": "www.cancertherapyadvisor.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"126749b77ad23fc5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChordoma - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"126749b77ad23fc5\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chordoma", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c24813eb3b1cea1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWith appropriate treatment, many chordoma patients will live for a decade or more, and some can be cured. In the United States, the annual incidence of chordoma is approximately <strong>1 in one million</strong> (300 new patients each year).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7c24813eb3b1cea1\">>>", "published": "December 22, 2025", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349052018}}
{"type": "message", "id": "ce436459", "parentId": "19a79c82", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:32.020Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:8", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"retinoblastoma annual cases United States children\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1103,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5bc63eb06b316f4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKey Statistics for Retinoblastoma | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5bc63eb06b316f4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/retinoblastoma/key-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5588286cd05a8a09\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma is a rare cancer of the eye. It is the most common tumor affecting the eye in children, and accounts for about 3% of all childhood cancers. <strong>About 300 –350</strong> cases are diagnosed in the United States each year.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5588286cd05a8a09\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 11, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c2dfc6a2cb236de5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c2dfc6a2cb236de5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545276/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"996ec56a9128b12c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe incidence ranges from 1 in 14,000 to 1 in 20,000 live births, with <strong>approximately 300 new cases diagnosed annually</strong> in the U.S.[25] While relatively rare, retinoblastoma’s potential for severe morbidity and mortality underscores the importance of understanding its epidemiological patterns.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"996ec56a9128b12c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 17, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6cadca4df84e512\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma in the United States: A 40-Year Incidence and Survival Analysis - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6cadca4df84e512\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29257183/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"076e6668a19340fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe annual incidence rates of retinoblastoma for a period of 40 years were <strong>12.14 (95% CI: 11.32 to 12.96) cases per 1 million children 4 years or younger</strong> and 0.49 (95% CI: 0.36 to 0.65) cases per 1 million children between the ages of 5 and 9 years.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"076e6668a19340fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"May 1, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a461f2cdeb5e657d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma Treatment (PDQ®) - NCI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a461f2cdeb5e657d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.gov/types/retinoblastoma/hp/retinoblastoma-treatment-pdq\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"94099c86a6dd71bd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTwo-thirds of all cases of retinoblastoma are diagnosed before age 2 years.[1] Thus, while the estimated annual incidence in the United States is approximately <strong>3 cases per 1 million children younger than 20 years</strong>, the age-adjusted annual incidence in children aged 0 to 4 years is 18.4 cases ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"94099c86a6dd71bd\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"248d9414de964164\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma | Children's Hospital Colorado\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"248d9414de964164\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.childrenscolorado.org/conditions-and-advice/conditions-and-symptoms/conditions/retinoblastoma/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc7e7d37a62d0370\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThere are <strong>approximately 350</strong> new cases of retinoblastoma every year in the United States. Retinoblastoma can affect one or both eyes, and in some cases involving both eyes, patients will also have a tumor in their pineal gland within their brain.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dc7e7d37a62d0370\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.childrenscolorado.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e7cfc86c546f8afa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e7cfc86c546f8afa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retinoblastoma\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4fd9a5b60f52ee8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma is extremely rare as there are only about <strong>200 to 300</strong> cases every year in the United States. Globally, only 1 in about 15,000 children have this malignancy, though rates continue to increase.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4fd9a5b60f52ee8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"3 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1d8f199e506003f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma - Definition, Symptoms, Diagnosis & Treatment Information | UT MD Anderson\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1d8f199e506003f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdanderson.org/cancer-types/retinoblastoma.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04684842ad06d8d6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma is a cancer of the retina, a light-sensitive layer of tissue in the eye. While it is rare, it is the most common malignant tumor that starts in the eye in children. Only <strong>about 350</strong> retinoblastoma cases are diagnosed each year in ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"04684842ad06d8d6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdanderson.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ffb6f51aea52c426\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe incidence of retinoblastoma in the United States: 1974 through 1985 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ffb6f51aea52c426\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2288550/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3f656e9e396f9378\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe incidence of retinoblastoma has been almost uniform form 1974 to 1985. The average annual incidence of retinoblastoma was <strong>5.8 per million for children younger than 10 years and 10.9 per million for children younger than 5 years</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3f656e9e396f9378\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28ef70c6c6cf50f0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma (Eye Cancer in Children) | Children's Hospital of Philadelphia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28ef70c6c6cf50f0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.chop.edu/conditions-diseases/retinoblastoma\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51f88ed7f6cf866d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe retina is a thin layer of nerve tissue that coats the back of the eye and enables the eye to see. Most cases (about 60 percent) involve only one eye (unilateral), but in some children, both eyes may be involved (bilateral). <strong>About 300</strong> children are diagnosed with retinoblastoma in the United ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51f88ed7f6cf866d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.chop.edu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"79ff0aebbd198d21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRetinoblastoma in the United States: A 40-Year Incidence and Survival Analysis | Journal of Pediatric Ophthalmology & Strabismus\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"79ff0aebbd198d21\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://journals.healio.com/doi/abs/10.3928/01913913-20171116-03\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93a4321e53f6180f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe annual incidence rates of retinoblastoma for a period of 40 years were <strong>12.14 (95% CI: 11.32 to 12.96) cases per 1 million children 4 years or younger</strong> and 0.49 (95% CI: 0.36 to 0.65) cases per 1 million children between the ages of 5 and 9 years.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93a4321e53f6180f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"journals.healio.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "retinoblastoma annual cases United States children", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1103, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5bc63eb06b316f4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nKey Statistics for Retinoblastoma | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5bc63eb06b316f4\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/retinoblastoma/key-statistics.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5588286cd05a8a09\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma is a rare cancer of the eye. It is the most common tumor affecting the eye in children, and accounts for about 3% of all childhood cancers. <strong>About 300 –350</strong> cases are diagnosed in the United States each year.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5588286cd05a8a09\">>>", "published": "September 11, 2025", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c2dfc6a2cb236de5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c2dfc6a2cb236de5\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK545276/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"996ec56a9128b12c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe incidence ranges from 1 in 14,000 to 1 in 20,000 live births, with <strong>approximately 300 new cases diagnosed annually</strong> in the U.S.[25] While relatively rare, retinoblastoma’s potential for severe morbidity and mortality underscores the importance of understanding its epidemiological patterns.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"996ec56a9128b12c\">>>", "published": "February 17, 2025", "siteName": "www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d6cadca4df84e512\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma in the United States: A 40-Year Incidence and Survival Analysis - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d6cadca4df84e512\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29257183/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"076e6668a19340fe\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe annual incidence rates of retinoblastoma for a period of 40 years were <strong>12.14 (95% CI: 11.32 to 12.96) cases per 1 million children 4 years or younger</strong> and 0.49 (95% CI: 0.36 to 0.65) cases per 1 million children between the ages of 5 and 9 years.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"076e6668a19340fe\">>>", "published": "May 1, 2018", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a461f2cdeb5e657d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma Treatment (PDQ®) - NCI\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a461f2cdeb5e657d\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.gov/types/retinoblastoma/hp/retinoblastoma-treatment-pdq", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94099c86a6dd71bd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTwo-thirds of all cases of retinoblastoma are diagnosed before age 2 years.[1] Thus, while the estimated annual incidence in the United States is approximately <strong>3 cases per 1 million children younger than 20 years</strong>, the age-adjusted annual incidence in children aged 0 to 4 years is 18.4 cases ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"94099c86a6dd71bd\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"248d9414de964164\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma | Children's Hospital Colorado\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"248d9414de964164\">>>", "url": "https://www.childrenscolorado.org/conditions-and-advice/conditions-and-symptoms/conditions/retinoblastoma/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc7e7d37a62d0370\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThere are <strong>approximately 350</strong> new cases of retinoblastoma every year in the United States. Retinoblastoma can affect one or both eyes, and in some cases involving both eyes, patients will also have a tumor in their pineal gland within their brain.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc7e7d37a62d0370\">>>", "siteName": "www.childrenscolorado.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e7cfc86c546f8afa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e7cfc86c546f8afa\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retinoblastoma", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f4fd9a5b60f52ee8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma is extremely rare as there are only about <strong>200 to 300</strong> cases every year in the United States. Globally, only 1 in about 15,000 children have this malignancy, though rates continue to increase.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f4fd9a5b60f52ee8\">>>", "published": "3 weeks ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1d8f199e506003f8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma - Definition, Symptoms, Diagnosis & Treatment Information | UT MD Anderson\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1d8f199e506003f8\">>>", "url": "https://www.mdanderson.org/cancer-types/retinoblastoma.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04684842ad06d8d6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma is a cancer of the retina, a light-sensitive layer of tissue in the eye. While it is rare, it is the most common malignant tumor that starts in the eye in children. Only <strong>about 350</strong> retinoblastoma cases are diagnosed each year in ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04684842ad06d8d6\">>>", "siteName": "www.mdanderson.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ffb6f51aea52c426\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe incidence of retinoblastoma in the United States: 1974 through 1985 - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ffb6f51aea52c426\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2288550/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3f656e9e396f9378\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe incidence of retinoblastoma has been almost uniform form 1974 to 1985. The average annual incidence of retinoblastoma was <strong>5.8 per million for children younger than 10 years and 10.9 per million for children younger than 5 years</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3f656e9e396f9378\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28ef70c6c6cf50f0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma (Eye Cancer in Children) | Children's Hospital of Philadelphia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28ef70c6c6cf50f0\">>>", "url": "https://www.chop.edu/conditions-diseases/retinoblastoma", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"51f88ed7f6cf866d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe retina is a thin layer of nerve tissue that coats the back of the eye and enables the eye to see. Most cases (about 60 percent) involve only one eye (unilateral), but in some children, both eyes may be involved (bilateral). <strong>About 300</strong> children are diagnosed with retinoblastoma in the United ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"51f88ed7f6cf866d\">>>", "siteName": "www.chop.edu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"79ff0aebbd198d21\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRetinoblastoma in the United States: A 40-Year Incidence and Survival Analysis | Journal of Pediatric Ophthalmology & Strabismus\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"79ff0aebbd198d21\">>>", "url": "https://journals.healio.com/doi/abs/10.3928/01913913-20171116-03", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93a4321e53f6180f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe annual incidence rates of retinoblastoma for a period of 40 years were <strong>12.14 (95% CI: 11.32 to 12.96) cases per 1 million children 4 years or younger</strong> and 0.49 (95% CI: 0.36 to 0.65) cases per 1 million children between the ages of 5 and 9 years.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93a4321e53f6180f\">>>", "siteName": "journals.healio.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349052019}}
{"type": "message", "id": "34433009", "parentId": "ce436459", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:32.111Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:9", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"small cell lung cancer 5 year survival rate\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1217,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3491c57634adb6d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | 5-Year Survival Rates for Lung Cancer | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3491c57634adb6d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/lung-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5b400fa713e7717\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe SEER database tracks 5-year relative survival rates for non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and small cell lung cancer (SCLC) in the United States, based on how far the cancer has spread. The SEER database, however, does not group cancers by AJCC TNM stages (stage 1, stage 2, stage 3, etc.).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5b400fa713e7717\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed4e0450a2fa11e1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer: A Review - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ed4e0450a2fa11e1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40163214/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a913bcfec1e3d767\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nImportance: Small cell lung cancer (SCLC) is a high-grade neuroendocrine carcinoma with an incidence of 4.7 cases per 100 000 individuals in 2021 in the US and a 5-year overall survival of <strong>12% to 30%</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a913bcfec1e3d767\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 3, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5d39ae17fa45d439\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurvival statistics for small cell lung cancer | Canadian Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5d39ae17fa45d439\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://cancer.ca/en/cancer-information/cancer-types/lung/prognosis-and-survival/small-cell-lung-cancer-survival-statistics\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ff46c667f0838f7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNet survival represents the probability (chance) of surviving cancer in the absence of other causes of death. It is used to give an estimate of the percentage of people who will survive cancer. <strong>In Canada, the 5-year net survival for lung cancer is 27%. This means that, on average, about 27%</strong> of ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ff46c667f0838f7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"cancer.ca\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0c5d060309d6db3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSmall cell lung cancer life expectancy: Stages and more\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0c5d060309d6db3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/small-cell-lung-cancer-life-expectancy\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"739fcf0dfd3f1e9c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLife expectancy for SCLC is <strong>lower compared to the general population</strong>, while survival rates are lower than those with nonsmall cell lung cancer. According to 2017 research, SCLC only accounts for about · 10–15% of lung cancers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"739fcf0dfd3f1e9c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 10, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.medicalnewstoday.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a9eb2d608669df7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSmall-cell carcinoma - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a9eb2d608669df7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small-cell_carcinoma\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"067e0ce341698f79\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2021, the FDA approved trilaciclib ... for small cell lung cancer (extensive and limited) range <strong>between 3.6% and 32.2% for women, and between 2.2% and 24.5% for men</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"067e0ce341698f79\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"4 days ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5777682772873ec\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | Lung Cancer Prognosis\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f5777682772873ec\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.lung-cancer.com/prognosis\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78918802b72169c1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWith aggressive treatment, the average life-span of limited-stage SCLC is 20 months. The 2-year survival rate in limited SCLC is 45%, and the 5-year survival rate is <strong>20%</strong> with treatment.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78918802b72169c1\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.lung-cancer.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"569b99639afc7dda\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLong-term survival in small-cell lung cancer\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"569b99639afc7dda\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7738624/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"98426ede9e94665c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChecking your browser before accessing pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov · Click here if you are not automatically redirected after 5 seconds\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"98426ede9e94665c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a3071286e707b086\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer Treatment (PDQ®) - NCI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a3071286e707b086\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.gov/types/lung/hp/small-cell-lung-treatment-pdq\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"39473e83dcafacd6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAbout 10% of people with SCLC remain ... risk of dying of lung cancer (both small and non-small cell types).[20] The overall survival rate at 5 years is <strong>5% to 10%</strong>.[1,20-22]...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"39473e83dcafacd6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6ab08386602aa8ec\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6ab08386602aa8ec\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482458/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6944c0a9f89ae1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEven with chemotherapy, the majority of patients are dead within 24 months, and <strong>less than 2%</strong> are alive at five years. For individuals with localized lung disease, treatment with chemotherapy and radiation does offer a better survival of 80% at two years, but less than 15% are alive at five years.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ca6944c0a9f89ae1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 10, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cab54018255ae71\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHow Long Do People With Small Cell Lung Cancer Survive?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cab54018255ae71\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.verywellhealth.com/small-cell-lung-cancer-survival-rates-2249295\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28529ef71d8b5ff1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDepending on the stage of cancer, the five-year survival rate for those with SCLC ranges from <strong>3% to 18%</strong>. While long-term disease-free survival is rare after a diagnosis of small cell lung cancer, it is possible.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28529ef71d8b5ff1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 27, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.verywellhealth.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "small cell lung cancer 5 year survival rate", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1217, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3491c57634adb6d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | 5-Year Survival Rates for Lung Cancer | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c3491c57634adb6d\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/lung-cancer/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5b400fa713e7717\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe SEER database tracks 5-year relative survival rates for non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and small cell lung cancer (SCLC) in the United States, based on how far the cancer has spread. The SEER database, however, does not group cancers by AJCC TNM stages (stage 1, stage 2, stage 3, etc.).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b5b400fa713e7717\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ed4e0450a2fa11e1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer: A Review - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ed4e0450a2fa11e1\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40163214/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a913bcfec1e3d767\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nImportance: Small cell lung cancer (SCLC) is a high-grade neuroendocrine carcinoma with an incidence of 4.7 cases per 100 000 individuals in 2021 in the US and a 5-year overall survival of <strong>12% to 30%</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a913bcfec1e3d767\">>>", "published": "June 3, 2025", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5d39ae17fa45d439\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSurvival statistics for small cell lung cancer | Canadian Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5d39ae17fa45d439\">>>", "url": "https://cancer.ca/en/cancer-information/cancer-types/lung/prognosis-and-survival/small-cell-lung-cancer-survival-statistics", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ff46c667f0838f7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNet survival represents the probability (chance) of surviving cancer in the absence of other causes of death. It is used to give an estimate of the percentage of people who will survive cancer. <strong>In Canada, the 5-year net survival for lung cancer is 27%. This means that, on average, about 27%</strong> of ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1ff46c667f0838f7\">>>", "siteName": "cancer.ca"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0c5d060309d6db3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSmall cell lung cancer life expectancy: Stages and more\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0c5d060309d6db3\">>>", "url": "https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/small-cell-lung-cancer-life-expectancy", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"739fcf0dfd3f1e9c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLife expectancy for SCLC is <strong>lower compared to the general population</strong>, while survival rates are lower than those with nonsmall cell lung cancer. According to 2017 research, SCLC only accounts for about · 10–15% of lung cancers.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"739fcf0dfd3f1e9c\">>>", "published": "June 10, 2021", "siteName": "www.medicalnewstoday.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a9eb2d608669df7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSmall-cell carcinoma - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a9eb2d608669df7\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small-cell_carcinoma", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"067e0ce341698f79\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn 2021, the FDA approved trilaciclib ... for small cell lung cancer (extensive and limited) range <strong>between 3.6% and 32.2% for women, and between 2.2% and 24.5% for men</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"067e0ce341698f79\">>>", "published": "4 days ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5777682772873ec\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLung Cancer Survival Rates | Lung Cancer Prognosis\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f5777682772873ec\">>>", "url": "https://www.lung-cancer.com/prognosis", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"78918802b72169c1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWith aggressive treatment, the average life-span of limited-stage SCLC is 20 months. The 2-year survival rate in limited SCLC is 45%, and the 5-year survival rate is <strong>20%</strong> with treatment.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"78918802b72169c1\">>>", "siteName": "www.lung-cancer.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"569b99639afc7dda\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLong-term survival in small-cell lung cancer\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"569b99639afc7dda\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7738624/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"98426ede9e94665c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nChecking your browser before accessing pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov · Click here if you are not automatically redirected after 5 seconds\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"98426ede9e94665c\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a3071286e707b086\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer Treatment (PDQ®) - NCI\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a3071286e707b086\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.gov/types/lung/hp/small-cell-lung-treatment-pdq", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"39473e83dcafacd6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAbout 10% of people with SCLC remain ... risk of dying of lung cancer (both small and non-small cell types).[20] The overall survival rate at 5 years is <strong>5% to 10%</strong>.[1,20-22]...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"39473e83dcafacd6\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6ab08386602aa8ec\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSmall Cell Lung Cancer - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6ab08386602aa8ec\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482458/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca6944c0a9f89ae1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEven with chemotherapy, the majority of patients are dead within 24 months, and <strong>less than 2%</strong> are alive at five years. For individuals with localized lung disease, treatment with chemotherapy and radiation does offer a better survival of 80% at two years, but less than 15% are alive at five years.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ca6944c0a9f89ae1\">>>", "published": "July 10, 2023", "siteName": "www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1cab54018255ae71\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHow Long Do People With Small Cell Lung Cancer Survive?\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1cab54018255ae71\">>>", "url": "https://www.verywellhealth.com/small-cell-lung-cancer-survival-rates-2249295", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28529ef71d8b5ff1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDepending on the stage of cancer, the five-year survival rate for those with SCLC ranges from <strong>3% to 18%</strong>. While long-term disease-free survival is rare after a diagnosis of small cell lung cancer, it is possible.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"28529ef71d8b5ff1\">>>", "published": "December 27, 2025", "siteName": "www.verywellhealth.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349052109}}
