is diagnosed at an early stage, and median survival for advanced ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c8677ee6cd4f7f34\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d03a0deb62ccca0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGallbladder Cancer | Penn State Health\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d03a0deb62ccca0\">>>", "url": "https://www.pennstatehealth.org/services-treatments/gallbladder-cancer", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"896fa559bce422cd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGallbladder cancer is relatively uncommon in the United States - about <strong>11,740 new cases per year</strong>, according to the American Cancer Society.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"896fa559bce422cd\">>>", "siteName": "www.pennstatehealth.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349070182}}
{"type": "message", "id": "bfdcbb6c", "parentId": "951722f5", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:17:50.189Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:14", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"vulvar cancer annual cases United States\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1012,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddeb645e843c5877\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Vulvar Cancer - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ddeb645e843c5877\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/vulva.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72587b4346b07ee0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIt is more common among women with a medical history of vulvar intraepithelial neoplasia, human papillomavirus (HPV) infection, or genital warts. The rate of new cases of vulvar cancer was <strong>2.6 per 100,000 women per year</strong> based on 2018–2022 ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72587b4346b07ee0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"584cdabaa57e26e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20‐Year Population‐Based Study - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"584cdabaa57e26e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11190582/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1eb3f3b9992a44b0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOne study in the United States reported a consistent <strong>1.2% annual rise in human papillomavirus (HPV)‐associated vulvar cancer cases [2]. Another study spanning from 2001 to 2018 noted an increase in overall vulvar cancer rates from 1.83 to 1.96 per 100 000 individuals</strong> [7].\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1eb3f3b9992a44b0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c09f54c44b0d4dc2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKey Statistics for Vulvar Cancer | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c09f54c44b0d4dc2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/vulvar-cancer/about/key-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa311d4f103f9a4f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the United States, vulvar cancer accounts for about <strong>0.7%</strong> of all cancers in women.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa311d4f103f9a4f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 13, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df7fdb9472482059\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nVaginal and Vulvar Cancer Statistics | Vaginal and Vulvar Cancers | CDC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df7fdb9472482059\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cdc.gov/vaginal-vulvar-cancers/statistics/index.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93d9f7a03e3d47be\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nVaginal and vulvar cancers are very rare. While all women are at risk for these cancers, very few will get them. The Data Visualizations tool makes it easy for anyone to explore and use the latest official federal government cancer data from United States Cancer Statistics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93d9f7a03e3d47be\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cdc.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3a0aac35cbda38e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nVulvar Cancer - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d3a0aac35cbda38e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK567798/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3b45256ca330016f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAccording to the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program, vulvar cancer represents 0.3% of all new cancer cases annually at a rate of <strong>2.6 per 100,000 women per year</strong> in the United States. Diagnosis is usually made in the sixth through eighth decades of life and is commonly ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3b45256ca330016f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 9, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e47260369bbe6456\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIs the incidence of invasive vulvar cancer increasing in the United States? - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e47260369bbe6456\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2868506/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8eac092bf53d3872\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe annual percentage change (APC) in incidence (and corresponding 95% confidence intervals) was computed, also using the SEER*Stat software. There were <strong>11,079 new in situ and 6,532 new invasive cases of vulvar cancer in the SEER population during 1973-2004</strong> (Table 1).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8eac092bf53d3872\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"18defe35803d039e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTrends in HPV- and non-HPV-associated vulvar cancer incidence, United States, 2001–2017 - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"18defe35803d039e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0091743522003516\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e084e7545253bcf0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>From 2001 to 2017, approximately 3500 cases of HPV-associated and 1000 cases of non-HPV-associated vulvar cancers occurred annually in the US</strong>. New cases of HPV-associated vulvar cancer increased from 2711 cases in 2001 to 4257 cases in 2017, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e084e7545253bcf0\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 12, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"faad74c7cc34466a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20‐Year Population‐Based Study - Mousavi - 2024 - Cancer Reports - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"faad74c7cc34466a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cnr2.2120\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f7b39e9eb12f8b95\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOne study in the United States reported a consistent <strong>1.2% annual rise in human papillomavirus (HPV)-associated vulvar cancer cases [2]. Another study spanning from 2001 to 2018 noted an increase in overall vulvar cancer rates from 1.83 to 1.96 per 100 000 individuals</strong> ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f7b39e9eb12f8b95\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 21, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1aefc4e046dd868f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nVulvar Cancer | UT MD Anderson\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1aefc4e046dd868f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdanderson.org/cancer-types/vulvar-cancer.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5d842e81b2d16e44\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLearn about vulvar cancer signs, diagnosis, causes, risk factors, and treatment options. Five-year survival rate: 71%. <strong>Annual diagnoses: 6,200.</strong> Median diagnosis age: 68.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5d842e81b2d16e44\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdanderson.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24b295e250707a3b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20-Year Population-Based Study - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24b295e250707a3b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39031816/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cefe45e40e949ccc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults: The age-adjusted incidence rate of vulvar cancer was <strong>2.40 (95% CI, 2.38-2.43) over the period 2000-2019</strong>, with an AAPC of 0.80 (95% CI, 0.63-0.99). By race/ethnicity, only non-Hispanic Whites had an increasing trend over 2000-2019 (AAPC: ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cefe45e40e949ccc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "vulvar cancer annual cases United States", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1012, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ddeb645e843c5877\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Stat Facts: Vulvar Cancer - SEER\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ddeb645e843c5877\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/vulva.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"72587b4346b07ee0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIt is more common among women with a medical history of vulvar intraepithelial neoplasia, human papillomavirus (HPV) infection, or genital warts. The rate of new cases of vulvar cancer was <strong>2.6 per 100,000 women per year</strong> based on 2018–2022 ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"72587b4346b07ee0\">>>", "siteName": "seer.cancer.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"584cdabaa57e26e0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20‐Year Population‐Based Study - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"584cdabaa57e26e0\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11190582/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1eb3f3b9992a44b0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOne study in the United States reported a consistent <strong>1.2% annual rise in human papillomavirus (HPV)‐associated vulvar cancer cases [2]. Another study spanning from 2001 to 2018 noted an increase in overall vulvar cancer rates from 1.83 to 1.96 per 100 000 individuals</strong> [7].\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1eb3f3b9992a44b0\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c09f54c44b0d4dc2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nKey Statistics for Vulvar Cancer | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c09f54c44b0d4dc2\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/vulvar-cancer/about/key-statistics.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aa311d4f103f9a4f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn the United States, vulvar cancer accounts for about <strong>0.7%</strong> of all cancers in women.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aa311d4f103f9a4f\">>>", "published": "January 13, 2026", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"df7fdb9472482059\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVaginal and Vulvar Cancer Statistics | Vaginal and Vulvar Cancers | CDC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"df7fdb9472482059\">>>", "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/vaginal-vulvar-cancers/statistics/index.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93d9f7a03e3d47be\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVaginal and vulvar cancers are very rare. While all women are at risk for these cancers, very few will get them. The Data Visualizations tool makes it easy for anyone to explore and use the latest official federal government cancer data from United States Cancer Statistics.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93d9f7a03e3d47be\">>>", "published": "June 10, 2025", "siteName": "www.cdc.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3a0aac35cbda38e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVulvar Cancer - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3a0aac35cbda38e\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK567798/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3b45256ca330016f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAccording to the Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program, vulvar cancer represents 0.3% of all new cancer cases annually at a rate of <strong>2.6 per 100,000 women per year</strong> in the United States. Diagnosis is usually made in the sixth through eighth decades of life and is commonly ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3b45256ca330016f\">>>", "published": "January 9, 2023", "siteName": "www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e47260369bbe6456\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIs the incidence of invasive vulvar cancer increasing in the United States? - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e47260369bbe6456\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2868506/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8eac092bf53d3872\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe annual percentage change (APC) in incidence (and corresponding 95% confidence intervals) was computed, also using the SEER*Stat software. There were <strong>11,079 new in situ and 6,532 new invasive cases of vulvar cancer in the SEER population during 1973-2004</strong> (Table 1).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8eac092bf53d3872\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"18defe35803d039e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTrends in HPV- and non-HPV-associated vulvar cancer incidence, United States, 2001–2017 - ScienceDirect\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"18defe35803d039e\">>>", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0091743522003516", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e084e7545253bcf0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>From 2001 to 2017, approximately 3500 cases of HPV-associated and 1000 cases of non-HPV-associated vulvar cancers occurred annually in the US</strong>. New cases of HPV-associated vulvar cancer increased from 2711 cases in 2001 to 4257 cases in 2017, ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e084e7545253bcf0\">>>", "published": "October 12, 2022", "siteName": "www.sciencedirect.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"faad74c7cc34466a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20‐Year Population‐Based Study - Mousavi - 2024 - Cancer Reports - Wiley Online Library\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"faad74c7cc34466a\">>>", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cnr2.2120", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f7b39e9eb12f8b95\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOne study in the United States reported a consistent <strong>1.2% annual rise in human papillomavirus (HPV)-associated vulvar cancer cases [2]. Another study spanning from 2001 to 2018 noted an increase in overall vulvar cancer rates from 1.83 to 1.96 per 100 000 individuals</strong> ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f7b39e9eb12f8b95\">>>", "published": "June 21, 2024", "siteName": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1aefc4e046dd868f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVulvar Cancer | UT MD Anderson\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1aefc4e046dd868f\">>>", "url": "https://www.mdanderson.org/cancer-types/vulvar-cancer.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5d842e81b2d16e44\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLearn about vulvar cancer signs, diagnosis, causes, risk factors, and treatment options. Five-year survival rate: 71%. <strong>Annual diagnoses: 6,200.</strong> Median diagnosis age: 68.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5d842e81b2d16e44\">>>", "siteName": "www.mdanderson.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24b295e250707a3b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIncidence Trends of Vulvar Cancer in the United States: A 20-Year Population-Based Study - PubMed\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"24b295e250707a3b\">>>", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39031816/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cefe45e40e949ccc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nResults: The age-adjusted incidence rate of vulvar cancer was <strong>2.40 (95% CI, 2.38-2.43) over the period 2000-2019</strong>, with an AAPC of 0.80 (95% CI, 0.63-0.99). By race/ethnicity, only non-Hispanic Whites had an increasing trend over 2000-2019 (AAPC: ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cefe45e40e949ccc\">>>", "siteName": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1776349070188}}
{"type": "message", "id": "2ef451ca", "parentId": "bfdcbb6c", "timestamp": "2026-04-16T14:18:02.721Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Now I have gathered sufficient information. Let me compile the response and write it to `answer.txt`."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "functions.write:15", "name": "write", "arguments": {"path": "/tmp/pinchbench/42b77639/agent_workspace/answer.txt", "content": "Cancer survival rates in the United States have shown significant improvement over recent decades, with the overall 5-year relative survival rate for all cancers combined reaching approximately 70% for diagnoses during 2015-2021, up from 58% in the mid-1970s. However, survival rates vary dramatically depending on the cancer type, stage at diagnosis, and available treatment options. Some cancers remain highly lethal due to late detection, aggressive biology, or limited therapeutic options, while others have seen remarkable advances in early detection and treatment. The following lists highlight five uncommon cancers with their annual incidence in the United States, followed by five of the most deadly cancers ranked by their 5-year survival rates.\n\nChordoma – approximately 300-350 cases per year\nRetinoblastoma – approximately 300-350 cases per year\nMerkel cell carcinoma – approximately 3,000 cases per year\nVulvar cancer – approximately 6,200 cases per year\nGallbladder cancer – approximately 11,740-12,640 cases per year\n\nGlioblastoma (5%)\nMesothelioma (5-10%)\nSmall cell lung cancer (5-10%)\nEsophageal cancer (19-22%)\nLiver cancer (22%)\n"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "qwen", "model": "kimi-k2.5", "usage": {"input": 25338, "output": 323, "cacheRead": 33280, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 58941, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1776349070191, "responseId": "chatcmpl-353b67eb-248f-91f1-9424-eed50ef9d93b"}}
